# Build outputs
out/
build.log

# live-build working artifacts (never commit; regenerated every build)
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, AND THAT MATTERS. These are live-build's own
# working directories, which it creates at the root of the config tree — which
# here is the repo root. Unanchored, `local/` matches a directory of that name
# at ANY depth, and it did: config/includes.chroot/usr/local/ is a real part of
# the shipped image (it is the XDG directory that takes priority over
# /usr/share/applications, which is how lynis.desktop hides Debian's dead
# launcher), so both files in it were untracked. build.sh rsyncs the working
# tree, so they reached the ISO from this checkout and nobody noticed — but a
# fresh clone would have built an image with no Family Limits launcher and
# Debian's broken Lynis entry back in the menu. Keep every pattern here
# anchored.
/.build/
/cache/
/chroot/
/binary/
/local/

# Test harness output
test/screen.png
/test/artifacts/

# Local audit, media, and scratch exports. These can contain large videos or
# synthetic migration/browser fixtures and must never ride along with a broad
# `git add -A`; keep the source scripts and manifests instead.
/output/
/outputs/
/tmp/

# Remotion promo: dependencies and rendered artifacts (keep the source)
promo/node_modules/
promo/out/
promo/.remotion/
/.remotion/

# Generated social-media renders and review output.  Keep the render scripts,
# manifests and narration source in Git; the binary delivery batches are
# reproducible output and make a release checkout enormous and non-reviewable.
/promo/review-batch/
/promo/launch-batch/
/promo/daily-fill-batch/
/promo/second-wave-batch/
/promo/instagram-launch-*/
/promo/linkedin-launch-*/
/promo/narration/audio/
/promo/public/narration-batch/
/promo/audit-work/

# Debian package staging mirrors config/includes.chroot and is rebuilt by
# packages/stage-packages.sh.  It must never become release source.
/pkgstage/

# Frame-transition evidence generated by the VM/UI review pass.
/test/transition-*.png
test/launcher-zoom.png
test/screen.png
.firebase/
/.wrangler/
/infra/.wrangler/

# Local-only credentials and key material — never commit.
#
# Broadened from two exact filenames to the shapes those files take, because
# naming one file only protects that one name. The repository is public, so a
# credential committed here is a credential published: rotate it, do not just
# delete the file, because the object survives in history.
r2-credentials.txt
r2.env
.env
.env.*
*-PRIVATE-*.asc
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
rclone.conf
# Cloudflare Wrangler's local secret store and config. .dev.vars holds the
# Stripe key while developing the gate Worker; wrangler.toml can carry account
# ids and bindings. Neither is currently in the tree — these are here so that
# creating one does not get staged by a `git add -A`.
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
wrangler.toml
# …with one deliberate exception. infra/wrangler.toml carries no account id and
# no secret — only the two R2 bucket names, which infra/README.md already states
# in this same repo. It has to be committed, because it is what makes a deploy
# SAFE: `wrangler deploy` replaces a worker's binding set with whatever the
# config declares, so deploying dagric-gate without a config that names the PRO
# binding would remove the private bucket holding the Pro ISO and break the
# download for every paying customer — silently, and in exchange for shipping a
# restyled error page. A config that only exists on one laptop is a config that
# is missing the day somebody else runs the deploy.
# If an account_id or a secret is ever added to it, delete this line first.
!infra/wrangler.toml

# Local editor/tooling settings. Personal to whoever is working on the tree and
# of no use to anyone cloning it.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Debug leftovers. Reading a Debian package's contents (to check what
# live-build actually does, or what a KDE theme actually ships) means
# `apt-get download` in whatever directory you happened to be in, and the .deb
# lands in the repo root. They are 200 KB each and belong to nobody.
# kde-style-breeze-data_4%3a6.3.5-1_all.deb was tracked from an earlier session
# and nothing referenced it; it has now been untracked, which is what this note
# used to ask for.
/*.deb

# The built APT repository. Regenerated in full by packages/build-repo.sh from
# config/includes.chroot, which is the single source of truth — committing it
# would add 5 MB of .deb to history on every release to store something that
# rebuilds in seconds. Build it before deploying the site.
site/repo/

# Python bytecode from tools/ — never belongs in the tree.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local credentials. Never committed, never pasted into a chat transcript.
.secrets/

# Windows occasionally expands a literal %SystemDrive% path inside the current
# directory when an old installer or cache task passes it through the wrong
# shell.  It is host cache data, never Dagric source, and can be very large.
/%SystemDrive%/
